WEBVTT

01:33.190 --> 01:36.650
Episode 7: Shake Half

01:54.460 --> 01:55.460
Yes?

01:56.090 --> 01:59.050
<i>Kobato-kun? It's me, Osanai.</i>

01:59.050 --> 02:00.180
What's wrong?

02:00.180 --> 02:03.100
<i>I sent you a message earlier.</i>

02:05.020 --> 02:09.020
I'm going to a shop between

02:05.020 --> 02:09.020
Laroche and Ginsendo today

02:05.020 --> 02:09.020
Meet me there at 3:30

02:10.270 --> 02:13.270
Laroche is here.

02:11.520 --> 02:13.480
<b>Laroche</b>

02:14.480 --> 02:16.070
Ginsendo is...

02:14.610 --> 02:16.530
<b>Ginsendo</b>

02:16.530 --> 02:17.440
Here.

02:19.530 --> 02:23.030
<b>Laroche</b>

02:19.530 --> 02:23.030
<b>Ginsendo</b>

02:19.530 --> 02:23.030
<b>Berry Berry
at San'yadori</b>

02:23.030 --> 02:25.330
Berry Berry at San'yadori.

02:30.040 --> 02:32.540
Berry Berry at San'yadori

02:30.040 --> 02:32.540
Frozen Watermelon Yogurt

02:30.040 --> 02:32.540
(whipped cream topping!)

02:37.630 --> 02:41.140
It's like we're in a relationship.

02:50.350 --> 02:53.860
<b>San'yadori 
Festival</b>

02:56.610 --> 02:58.610
<b>Reggae</b>

02:56.610 --> 02:58.610
<b>Festival</b>

03:01.360 --> 03:03.370
<b>San'yadori 
Festival</b>

03:01.360 --> 03:03.370
<b>San'yadori 
Festival</b>

03:01.360 --> 03:03.370
<b>Reggae</b>

03:01.360 --> 03:03.370
<b>Festival</b>

03:03.370 --> 03:07.120
<b>Takoyaki</b>

03:10.040 --> 03:12.120
We're meeting up at 3:30.

03:28.520 --> 03:29.350
Yo.

03:31.980 --> 03:34.360
Hey. I haven't seen you 
since the pastry incident.

03:34.360 --> 03:36.110
Thanks for your help with that.

03:46.990 --> 03:48.410
You here to investigate, too?

03:48.990 --> 03:50.200
Investigate what?

03:50.200 --> 03:51.250
You aren't?

03:51.830 --> 03:53.870
I'm just here for a bite.

03:54.710 --> 03:57.250
Looks like <i>you're</i> 
investigating something, Kengo.

03:57.750 --> 03:58.500
Yeah.

03:59.260 --> 04:01.010
But it's none of your business.

04:03.510 --> 04:06.100
It has to do with 
a female student at school.

04:06.100 --> 04:11.850
I can't tell you who, but it seems 
she's been roped into joining a group.

04:12.230 --> 04:13.560
What kind of group?

04:14.350 --> 04:15.940
Illicit drug users.

04:16.610 --> 04:20.570
Run by some kid who's been 
doing 'em since middle school.

04:22.030 --> 04:24.950
The girl's kid sister asked me to help.

04:25.360 --> 04:28.580
She's desperate to find a way
 to get her out of there.

04:33.160 --> 04:37.840
I don't have much info. 
I'm still just trying to learn about the group.

04:38.920 --> 04:40.090
Drugs, you say?

04:40.710 --> 04:43.630
They started off with 
cough syrup and sleeping aids.

04:44.220 --> 04:46.300
I need to investigate more on that, too.

04:46.760 --> 04:48.510
So you're staking them out?

04:49.350 --> 04:50.640
You sound interested.

04:51.390 --> 04:53.270
No, not at all.

04:56.940 --> 04:59.650
Do you have a plan for how 
to get her out of the group?

05:00.020 --> 05:02.530
I'm gonna find the group's hideout...

05:02.530 --> 05:03.490
Uh-huh.

05:03.490 --> 05:05.400
...and beat 'em with a wooden sword.

05:07.030 --> 05:08.320
I'm kidding.

05:11.080 --> 05:14.040
I don't know what Kawamata 
Sanae wants herself yet.

05:15.000 --> 05:17.960
Whether she was dragged in 
against her will as Kasumi says,

05:17.960 --> 05:21.000
or if she joined because she wanted to...

05:22.300 --> 05:24.970
Speaking of which, Kengo, 
at my middle school...

05:25.340 --> 05:26.260
They're moving.

05:27.300 --> 05:28.300
Where?

05:30.800 --> 05:33.310
Damn. They split up.

05:39.310 --> 05:42.440
Jogoro, could you do me a favor?

05:42.440 --> 05:45.150
Keep an eye on them for 
as much time as you can spare.

05:45.150 --> 05:46.820
Uh, sure.

05:47.320 --> 05:49.160
Then contact this person.

05:49.530 --> 05:50.450
Later.

05:53.120 --> 05:54.660
He sure goes deep.

06:02.130 --> 06:02.920
What's this?

06:07.800 --> 06:10.050
Hello, it's me, Osanai-san

06:12.550 --> 06:12.850
Hello, it's me, Osanai-san

06:12.810 --> 06:14.810
I'm right behind you

06:12.850 --> 06:12.930
Hello, it's me, Osanai-san

06:12.930 --> 06:14.810
Hello, it's me, Osanai-san

06:19.140 --> 06:21.150
That's a unique look.

06:21.150 --> 06:22.520
Doesn't it suit me?

06:22.520 --> 06:23.730
It kinda does.

06:24.230 --> 06:26.650
Actually, I'm not sure 
how I feel about that.

06:31.370 --> 06:34.410
You worked out I was 
talking about Berry Berry.

06:35.290 --> 06:36.660
It wasn't that hard.

06:38.750 --> 06:41.670
I knew you would figure it out, Kobato-kun.

06:43.090 --> 06:45.920
What were you talking to Dojima-kun about?

06:49.380 --> 06:51.510
A group of druggies.

06:51.970 --> 06:54.010
Remember in middle school?

06:54.560 --> 06:55.720
Yeah.

06:55.720 --> 06:57.180
Isawa Hasemi-san.

06:57.520 --> 06:59.100
You know about her?

06:59.560 --> 07:02.060
Anyway, it's a group like that,

07:02.060 --> 07:05.480
and Kengo's girlfriend's 
older sister got roped into joining.

07:06.900 --> 07:12.320
Do you think this Isawa-san is involved 
in the group Kengo's talking about?

07:16.290 --> 07:19.410
Isawa-san got put on probation,

07:19.410 --> 07:22.330
but I don't think she thinks 
she did anything wrong.

07:23.080 --> 07:27.500
We can't assume there's 
only one such group, though.

07:27.960 --> 07:30.050
So I don't know.

07:30.840 --> 07:32.760
By the way, what's that?

07:33.890 --> 07:34.850
"Han"?

07:35.220 --> 07:40.350
Kengo wants me to kill some time here, 
then contact this person.

07:40.980 --> 07:44.480
Is that a secret code between you two?

07:44.480 --> 07:47.400
Nope. I have no idea what it is.

07:49.360 --> 07:52.610
A place with the character "han" 
in the name? Or a person, maybe?

07:53.160 --> 07:56.530
There's a place called Hanzawa-cho 
in this town, isn't there?

07:57.080 --> 08:00.080
Not that I've ever been 
to that area with Kengo.

08:00.950 --> 08:05.540
Hmm, there was a Hanmura 
in our class in middle school.

08:05.540 --> 08:09.380
But that was someone Kengo hardly 
knew and who I never spoke to.

08:11.340 --> 08:12.420
Half.

08:12.880 --> 08:14.390
"Fifty-fifty."

08:14.800 --> 08:16.470
50-50.

08:18.470 --> 08:20.930
If it was that, he could've just written 5050.

08:21.270 --> 08:25.690
And 5050 isn't even a valid phone number.

08:25.690 --> 08:28.690
You're right. We're on the wrong path.

08:29.150 --> 08:32.070
What did Dojima-kun say 
when he left you with this?

08:34.200 --> 08:37.070
"Contact them. Please."

08:37.450 --> 08:40.830
So "Han" has to be some kind of contact?

08:41.200 --> 08:43.580
I didn't really get much out of him.

08:44.000 --> 08:46.830
If he wanted me to contact him at "half"...

08:47.790 --> 08:49.590
It's three right now.

08:50.300 --> 08:53.170
Maybe he wants you to contact him at 3:30?

08:53.170 --> 08:54.760
Do you really think that?

08:56.220 --> 08:59.720
He could've just told you
 to call him at 3:30.

09:02.560 --> 09:08.520
The nature of this "Han" is such that 
there's too much info to communicate orally.

09:10.070 --> 09:14.320
I suspect that's where 
the key to this message lies.

09:17.910 --> 09:19.330
It's odd, though.

09:19.330 --> 09:20.450
What is?

09:20.870 --> 09:23.700
The first and second 
strokes are slightly off.

09:24.790 --> 09:30.000
The left flick that goes through the vertical 
stroke. The second horizontal is shorter.

09:31.800 --> 09:34.590
You're right. The stroke order seems odd.

09:34.590 --> 09:35.670
I've got it.

09:36.720 --> 09:38.140
It's a map.

09:38.510 --> 09:40.300
These are two intersections.

09:40.300 --> 09:42.890
He put a check mark 
on the second intersection.

09:44.060 --> 09:47.230
Kengo wants me to contact the person here.

09:47.850 --> 09:50.110
But where is it?

09:50.770 --> 09:53.650
It's a map, which means there 
should be an origin somewhere.

09:56.240 --> 09:57.610
What's wrong?

09:57.610 --> 10:00.490
No, I just realized I've done it again.

10:03.580 --> 10:06.250
Kobato-kun, remember what you said?

10:06.250 --> 10:12.250
You said an ordinary person wouldn't cause 
trouble by refusing an acquaintance's request.

10:13.590 --> 10:15.510
Yeah. You're right.

10:17.220 --> 10:19.260
I've been thinking...

10:21.050 --> 10:25.310
You had a hard time reframing the problem 
because you had certain expectations

10:25.310 --> 10:27.690
about what Dojima-kun might do.

10:29.140 --> 10:32.940
All right. I'll stop underestimating Kengo.

10:34.400 --> 10:36.320
A map needs an origin point.

10:36.820 --> 10:39.870
And Kengo drew this for me earlier,

10:39.870 --> 10:43.120
assuming I'd definitely understand it.

10:46.370 --> 10:48.750
No, he didn't hand it to me.

10:48.750 --> 10:51.130
I picked it up from where he left it.

11:02.510 --> 11:04.680
You brought a change of clothes?

11:04.680 --> 11:05.350
Yep.

11:07.350 --> 11:09.310
Oh. It's this shop.

11:08.270 --> 11:10.770
<b>Muramatsuya</b>

11:10.520 --> 11:13.150
Their candy apples 
were on your ranked list.

11:12.520 --> 11:14.020
Muramatsuya

11:12.520 --> 11:14.020
Candy apples

11:12.520 --> 11:14.020
*Note sale date!*

11:15.690 --> 11:17.360
I'm happy you remembered.

11:23.740 --> 11:24.990
That way.

11:34.420 --> 11:35.920
Hello.

11:35.920 --> 11:38.550
Dojima Kengo asked me to come here.

11:39.010 --> 11:41.050
Did something happen to Kenken?

11:43.590 --> 11:48.310
I don't really know, either, 
but Kenken seems to have found something.

11:48.310 --> 11:50.100
He went chasing after someone.

11:50.850 --> 11:52.270
I see.

11:53.150 --> 11:54.810
And where is he now?

11:54.810 --> 11:58.570
I don't know. That's all I have.

11:58.900 --> 12:00.110
Well, good luck.

12:08.620 --> 12:10.500
Hey, Kobato-kun.

12:14.040 --> 12:16.840
Today's frozen watermelon yogurt...

12:18.340 --> 12:20.550
It's on me.

12:24.970 --> 12:27.510
<b>Kobato Japanese Confectionery</b>

12:49.330 --> 12:50.370
Hello?

12:50.370 --> 12:52.290
<i>Is this Kobato-kun's residence?</i>

12:52.290 --> 12:53.710
<i>My name's Dojima.</i>

12:53.710 --> 12:55.080
Oh, it's you, Kengo.

12:55.500 --> 12:57.750
<i>I'm going out for tanmen. Join me.</i>

13:06.680 --> 13:09.680
<b>Tantan
Kinryu</b>

13:08.510 --> 13:10.850
Sorry for dragging you out.

13:10.850 --> 13:12.470
It's on me today.

13:12.470 --> 13:13.980
Why, thank you.

13:13.980 --> 13:16.310
You weren't doing anything anyway, were you?

13:16.310 --> 13:19.980
I'm pretty busy this summer, 
believe it or not.

13:19.980 --> 13:22.360
Osanai-san keeps taking me out.

13:22.360 --> 13:23.740
Today, it's parfaits.

13:23.740 --> 13:25.700
Tomorrow, it's sundaes.

13:26.160 --> 13:28.200
I'm glad you're so close.

13:30.160 --> 13:32.950
So what's the reason for 
bringing me out here?

13:33.370 --> 13:37.960
You're the second best thing to vent at.

13:37.960 --> 13:39.080
What's number one?

13:39.080 --> 13:41.340
Digging a hole and yelling into it.

13:43.010 --> 13:46.760
Then why don't you just
 talk to your girlfriend?

13:46.760 --> 13:48.640
Kawamata-san, wasn't it?

13:49.010 --> 13:51.430
Kawamata isn't my girlfriend.

13:53.060 --> 13:55.640
How do you know Kawamata?

13:55.640 --> 13:57.980
You told me about her the other day.

13:57.980 --> 13:59.060
I did?

13:59.060 --> 14:02.690
You told me that Kawamata 
Sanae-san's sister, uh...

14:03.070 --> 14:07.030
Kawamata Kasumi-san asked you to help.

14:07.570 --> 14:09.530
I told you all that?

14:10.530 --> 14:14.450
So? What's become of our young lady...

14:14.450 --> 14:15.580
"Kenken"?

14:20.290 --> 14:24.960
I told you she's been trying to get her sister
 to leave this real nasty group, right?

14:24.960 --> 14:25.840
You did.

14:27.590 --> 14:29.210
I got kicked out.

14:30.220 --> 14:35.020
But if she joined of her own free will,
 there's nothing we can do.

14:36.390 --> 14:40.600
If she were the type who enjoyed doing 
recreational drugs, I'd leave her be.

14:41.110 --> 14:44.650
But Kawamata's <i>trying</i> to leave.

14:46.150 --> 14:51.160
Jogoro, back in Takaba Middle School, 
was anyone arrested for doing drugs?

14:51.160 --> 14:54.330
Yeah. I thought about 
telling you the other day.

14:56.000 --> 14:59.420
The leader who got taken in was named Isawa.

14:59.420 --> 15:03.630
She suspected Kawamata of ratting her out.

15:04.340 --> 15:08.170
She's apparently made some very real threats
 since finding Kawamata this year.

15:08.920 --> 15:10.470
Threats?

15:10.470 --> 15:13.850
She came at her with a wrench.

15:15.100 --> 15:19.350
Apparently, Kawamata didn't rat her out, 
but she's completely terrified now.

15:19.350 --> 15:21.770
She can't leave the group 
even though she wants to.

15:22.860 --> 15:24.320
But the thing is...

15:25.480 --> 15:27.990
Kawamata won't believe me at all.

15:28.490 --> 15:33.700
At first, she thought Isawa was using me
 to see if she was the traitor.

15:33.700 --> 15:35.830
Her sister asked you to help, didn't she?

15:36.200 --> 15:38.450
Why didn't you mention her name?

15:38.790 --> 15:42.750
I did, of course. I had her prove it, too.

15:43.380 --> 15:47.920
Then she asked, "Are you 
going to protect me 24/7?"

15:48.420 --> 15:53.720
"Isawa's unhinged. She might 
murder me if I leave unannounced."

15:54.010 --> 15:57.060
And now you're depressed.

15:57.060 --> 15:59.680
I was hoping there would 
be something I could do.

15:59.680 --> 16:01.270
So I went to see her again.

16:02.270 --> 16:06.150
Now, Jogoro, what do you think she told me?

16:06.150 --> 16:08.690
That she doesn't 
appreciate it or something?

16:08.690 --> 16:09.570
Nope.

16:10.530 --> 16:12.490
That I'm in her way.

16:13.490 --> 16:14.370
"In her way"?

16:14.870 --> 16:19.240
I don't care about helping Kawamata Sanae 
so much that I'll take shit for trying.

16:20.000 --> 16:21.370
That's just egotism.

16:23.710 --> 16:25.880
Hey, these things happen.

16:26.920 --> 16:29.340
I'm glad I talked to you.

16:30.210 --> 16:35.090
I figured you'd just nod along 
without sympathizing too much.

16:36.180 --> 16:37.350
Order up!

16:37.350 --> 16:40.140
Extra spicy, extra large tanmen.

16:41.680 --> 16:45.270
Well, Jogoro? How can you 
<i>not</i> binge at a time like this?

16:45.270 --> 16:49.110
And what could be better than 
this tanmen when you need to binge?

16:49.110 --> 16:51.900
Okay. I get it. Just eat.

16:52.780 --> 16:55.410
Well, let's dig in.

16:55.410 --> 16:58.580
Excuse me. Could I get 
two extra large bowls of fried rice, too?

16:58.580 --> 17:01.700
Sure thing. Two extra large bowls
 of fried rice coming up!

17:02.080 --> 17:04.710
That isn't for me, is it?

17:20.680 --> 17:24.180
<b>Calling</b>

17:20.680 --> 17:24.180
Osanai Yuki

17:22.810 --> 17:25.520
She doesn't usually call this late.

17:26.400 --> 17:27.600
Hello?

17:27.600 --> 17:30.650
<i>Oh, Kobato-kun? Sorry for calling so late.</i>

17:30.650 --> 17:31.860
It's fine.

17:32.480 --> 17:34.490
It's hot tonight, isn't it?

17:34.490 --> 17:37.410
I don't think I'll be able to sleep much.

17:37.410 --> 17:39.330
<i>You could go get some fresh air.</i>

17:40.280 --> 17:41.870
So did you need something?

17:41.870 --> 17:43.450
<i>Yeah, actually.</i>

17:44.080 --> 17:50.340
<i>Hey, we talked about going to
 the San'yadori Festival together, right?</i>

17:50.340 --> 17:51.420
Oh, yeah.

17:51.960 --> 17:53.420
We're good, right?

17:53.840 --> 17:54.970
<i>Yeah, I'll be free.</i>

17:54.970 --> 17:57.050
Okay. That's great.

17:57.430 --> 17:59.220
I wasn't sure...

17:59.220 --> 18:00.930
<i>...I'd asked you properly.</i>

18:00.930 --> 18:04.930
I hate to say it, but it's just an ordinary 
shopping district festival, isn't it?

18:04.930 --> 18:09.230
<i>Actually, there's a 
Muramatsuya in San'yadori.</i>

18:09.610 --> 18:13.230
<i>That's the number one place 
to buy Japanese snacks in town.</i>

18:13.230 --> 18:14.820
<i>That's basic knowledge.</i>

18:14.820 --> 18:16.950
It's their candy apples you like, right?

18:16.950 --> 18:20.530
<i>Yeah. Candy apples are
 technically cheap sweets,</i>

18:20.530 --> 18:23.870
<i>so they don't really go 
under my sweets selection.</i>

18:23.870 --> 18:26.960
But Muramatsuya's 
candy apples are different.

18:26.960 --> 18:28.870
Got that, Kobato-kun?

18:28.870 --> 18:30.580
<i>Totally different.</i>

18:31.290 --> 18:32.630
Uh-huh.

18:33.000 --> 18:39.680
<i>They sell special candy apples at the 
San'yadori Festival. Just one day a year.</i>

18:40.590 --> 18:43.720
<i>They prepare an especially tart variety,</i>

18:43.720 --> 18:46.600
<i>and start peeling after 
the customer's made an order.</i>

18:47.640 --> 18:51.230
<i>The balance between sour and sweet...</i>

18:51.810 --> 18:56.150
<i>It elevates the concept of 
the candy apple to the next level.</i>

18:56.610 --> 18:58.030
I see.

18:58.400 --> 19:03.030
<i>I've introduced you to a lot of shops
 this summer, haven't I?</i>

19:03.410 --> 19:07.710
<i>But until I get you to
try these candy apples,</i>

19:07.710 --> 19:11.420
<i>I won't have introduced you 
to anything </i>truly<i> valuable.</i>

19:11.420 --> 19:13.030
Well, I can't wait.

19:13.540 --> 19:16.170
Are we meeting there tomorrow?

19:16.680 --> 19:19.270
<i>We'll meet up at my place first.</i>

19:19.270 --> 19:21.690
<i>Then we'll go there together.</i>

19:22.060 --> 19:25.350
Okay. Be at my place by around one.

19:26.260 --> 19:28.400
One. Got it.

19:28.400 --> 19:29.560
<i>Promise.</i>

19:30.500 --> 19:35.410
This is the culmination of 
our memories this summer.

19:47.740 --> 19:50.130
Welcome. You must be Kobato-san.

19:50.420 --> 19:53.350
Oh, nice to meet you. I'm Kobato.

19:53.760 --> 19:57.500
I'm sorry, but she's out.

19:58.170 --> 20:00.600
She should be back soon.

20:00.600 --> 20:04.420
She asked me to get you to 
come in and wait when you arrive.

20:04.420 --> 20:06.030
Oh, I...

20:08.300 --> 20:11.190
Thank you for being so good to Yuki.

20:11.190 --> 20:13.270
Oh, she's been great to me, too.

20:17.250 --> 20:20.020
You look like an upright person. I'm glad.

20:22.080 --> 20:27.670
She seems to be on the phone a lot
at night since summer break started.

20:27.670 --> 20:30.900
I was sure she'd found a good friend.

20:31.600 --> 20:34.610
I was surprised it was a boy, though.

20:37.100 --> 20:40.250
Do you know where 
Osanai-san might have gone?

20:40.250 --> 20:44.200
She left before noon saying 
she had some shopping to do.

20:44.200 --> 20:45.700
I'm sorry.

20:45.700 --> 20:47.530
Before noon?

20:49.280 --> 20:50.300
Oh?

20:50.300 --> 20:51.810
Excuse me a second.

20:53.640 --> 20:55.640
Hello, Osanai residence.

21:01.530 --> 21:03.310
Who are you?

21:05.120 --> 21:07.030
Wait. Where is she?

21:11.640 --> 21:12.960
Has something happened?

21:14.700 --> 21:17.760
She's... Yuki's...

21:19.660 --> 21:22.310
They want five million in exchange for her.

21:22.920 --> 21:25.290
It was a strange modulated voice.

21:26.210 --> 21:31.600
You mean... Osanai-san's been abducted?
